::SECTION_45_XML_SITEMAPS_AND_STRUCTURED_SCHEMAS::
@FAULT_NODE [ERR-XML-001] {
    DOMAIN          : "Recursive XML Sitemap & Event Manifest Generation (JOE-TRON / EV.4.*.xml)"
    PHENOMENON      : "XML parser fatal entity errors, broken `<loc>` URLs with raw `&` or `<` characters, or >50,000-node sitemap rejection"
    ROOT_CAUSE      : "Interpolating raw filesystem paths or query parameters into XML tags without entity escaping (`&amp;`, `&lt;`, `&gt;`, `&quot;`, `&apos;`), or exceeding XML sitemap protocol size/node limits."
    INVARIANT_RULE  : "Escape all five XML predefined entities on every interpolated path/value, emit UTF-8 `<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>` headers, and split sitemaps automatically before reaching 50,000 URLs or 50MB uncompressed."
}

::SECTION_46_MONOTONIC_TIMERS_AND_DELTA_STEPPING::
@FAULT_NODE [ERR-TMR-001] {
    DOMAIN          : "High-Resolution Performance Counters & Simulation Frame Stepping (QueryPerformanceCounter)"
    PHENOMENON      : "Negative delta-time jumps on NTP clock sync, physics/animation explosion after window drag pauses, or 32-bit `GetTickCount()` 49.7-day wraparound"
    ROOT_CAUSE      : "Using wall-clock `GetSystemTimeAsFileTime` or `GetTickCount()` for frame/poll intervals, or passing unclamped `dt` values into simulation loops."
    INVARIANT_RULE  : "Compute intervals exclusively via monotonic `QueryPerformanceCounter` divided by `QueryPerformanceFrequency`, and clamp frame `dt` to a hard ceiling (e.g., `dt <= 0.1f`) to survive OS modal drag stalls."
}

::SECTION_47_SHELL_DRAG_DROP_AND_CLIPBOARD_HANDLES::
@FAULT_NODE [ERR-SHL-001] {
    DOMAIN          : "Win32 Drag-and-Drop Ingestion & Global Clipboard Memory (DragQueryFileW / GlobalLock)"
    PHENOMENON      : "Truncated Unicode filenames, leaked `HDROP` handles, or heap corruption from writing directly to `OpenClipboard` pointers"
    ROOT_CAUSE      : "Using ANSI `DragQueryFileA` on Unicode paths, omitting `DragFinish(hDrop)`, or calling `GlobalFree()` on handles already owned by `SetClipboardData()`."
    INVARIANT_RULE  : "Query required buffer length via `DragQueryFileW(hDrop, i, NULL, 0)`, copy paths into wide buffers, always call `DragFinish(hDrop)`, and transfer `GMEM_MOVEABLE` ownership cleanly to `SetClipboardData` without freeing post-handoff."
}

::MASTER_VERIFICATION_GATE::
@GATE_CHECK_F15 {
    47. XML_ENTITY_PURE    : Escape all 5 XML entities in `<loc>` and manifest nodes and enforce 50k-URL partition bounds.
    48. MONOTONIC_DT_CLAMP : Drive timers via `QueryPerformanceCounter` and clamp delta-time spikes across modal window stalls.
    49. HDROP_CLIP_HYGIENE : Use wide `DragQueryFileW` with mandatory `DragFinish()` and respect `GMEM_MOVEABLE` clipboard ownership transfer.
}
